<title>UK: GKN no comment on legal case, shares recover.</title>
<headline>GKN no comment on legal case, shares recover.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK engineering group GKN Plc saw its shares rebound on Friday after falling sharply on Thursday on renewed fears about the U.S. litigation involving its franchise operation Meineke Discount Muffler Shops Inc.</p>
<p>The shares were up 19 1/2 pence at 955 after falling 28 1/2 pence to 935 1/2 in the last session.</p>
<p>But GKN said it would be making no comment on the source of the turbulence -- a Meineke representative at the AGM. He had told the Thursday meeting that some franchisees who had signed waivers as part of their contracts still planned to continue to seek damages for alleged misuse of advertising funds.</p>
</text>
